Found while writing the consumer skills perl-crypt-age, perl-file-sops and perl-net-async-kubernetes (their boards k50, k205, k82):

- lib/OCP/Keys.pm line 478 says the password layer runs "via Crypt::Age password mode". Crypt::Age has no passphrase mode; the layer is OCP's own PBKDF2 + AES-GCM (_double_encrypt), age-encrypted to recipients afterwards. The comment should say that.
- lib/OCP.pm lines 74-90 (quote_sops_lastmodified) rest on "File::SOPS before 0.004 emits lastmodified bare". Only 0.002 wrote it bare; 0.003 and later write it quoted, and the cpanfile pins File::SOPS 0.005. quote_sops_lastmodified and its five call sites (Keys.pm 613, Secrets.pm 677, 784, 910, 967) can go; a document still carrying a bare value is rewritten by File::SOPS->rotate.
- lib/OCP/Robocop/Controller.pm lines 113-116 and 404-408 say the watcher retries every second without a word. Net::Async::Kubernetes::Watcher backs off from 1s to 30s and reports every failed attempt to on_error (warn without one); it retries forever unless max_retries is set, so the API check stays useful. Wiring on_error into robocop's logging makes a broken watch visible on its own.

Done when: the comments describe the libraries as they are, and the lastmodified workaround is gone with its test adjusted.

